Drawer: captured free component source. Panel that slides in from any edge over a dimmed page, for filters, details and bottom sheets, sharing Modal's header, body and actions.

Primary source: components/base/drawer/drawer.tsx. Exported names: DrawerPlacement, DrawerSize, DrawerProps, Drawer, DrawerBody, DrawerFooter, DrawerHeader, DrawerTrigger, DrawerBodyProps, DrawerHeaderProps, DrawerTriggerProps.

Declared npm dependencies: react-aria-components@^1.17.0.

BoardUI registry dependencies: cx, direction, modal. These names refer to source registry items, not npm packages.

Types from the primary source (referenced types may be imported):

```tsx
export type DrawerPlacement = "start" | "end" | "top" | "bottom";

export type DrawerSize = "sm" | "md" | "lg";

export interface DrawerProps extends Omit<ModalOverlayProps, "children" | "className" | "style"> {
  /** The edge the panel slides in from. `start` and `end` follow the reading direction. */
  placement?: DrawerPlacement;
  /** Width of a start or end drawer: 320, 400 (default), or 600px. */
  size?: DrawerSize;
  /** Accessible name when the content has no DrawerHeader title. */
  "aria-label"?: string;
  /** Classes on the panel surface. */
  className?: string;
  /** Classes on the full-screen overlay. */
  overlayClassName?: string;
  children: ReactNode | ((renderProps: DialogRenderProps) => ReactNode);
}
```

